WHAT THIS FILE ESTABLISHES

  The console evidence for probe query three: the PARAMETERIZED form of the
  handler-to-privileged-launch question, instantiated on TWO named handler/sink
  pairs in ONE run. It is one of the four heap-bound JVM invocations this run
  records separately - the jimple2cpg frontend build, the importCpg verification
  load, the Stage 3 Joern runner, and this probe.

  IT IS ALSO WHERE ONE OF THE PROBE'S THREE EFFORT MEASURES IS SETTLED.
  Parameterizability passes ONLY because the query was actually invoked on the
  SECOND named pair and that invocation's result was captured; a parameter list
  that merely exists does not satisfy it. Queries 01 and 02 both defer the
  measure to this file and assert nothing about it. So this file is not a summary
  of a capability - it is the place where the capability was exercised, and
  PHASE 5 is that exercise with the second pair's own numbers.

  It carries, in execution order: the preconditions that had to hold before the
  query was allowed to load the graph, the target surface measured in the pinned
  tree rather than assumed, the exact command with its JDK major version and the
  heap it actually received as three separate fields, what the query reported per
  pair, the second pair's invocation and result, all three effort measures named
  individually, the duplicate-formulation verdict against BOTH siblings reasoned
  on substance, the spurious-route definition with its selectors quoted verbatim,
  the cross-checks, and the terminal transcript verbatim.

  The <nn>-<slug> in this file's name matches the query source exactly:
  queries/joern/03-parameterized-handler-sink-pairs.sc. The slug is the one the
  plan names - parameterized-handler-sink-pairs.

  WHAT THIS FILE IS NOT. It is OBSERVATIONAL. It is not a finding, and nothing in
  it is an assessment of Spark, of any Spark component or of any Spark
  configuration. It judges no finding - not real, not important, not a false
  positive, not a duplicate of another tool's - and it makes no comparison
  between tools, which is why no other scanner is named anywhere in it. It
  contributes NO row to oss-scan-results/findings.json and writes nothing into
  harness/artifacts/raw/; PHASE 9 measures both of those rather than asserting
  them. Joern appears twice in this run by design: once as one of the nine
  scanned runners, and once as the subject of this probe. Nothing here is added
  to, merged with or compared against that runner's output, and no figure in this
  file is arithmetic over the two.

  AND NO TWO OF ITS NUMBERS ARE EVER ADDED TOGETHER. Two pairs in one run invite
  the reader to sum their returns; two sibling queries over pair one invite the
  same. Every route count in this file is reported PER PAIR, and no arithmetic
  anywhere in it combines one pair with the other, or either with query 01's or
  query 02's returns.

