  STEP 7 OF 9 - THE HEAP, PROVEN COMMITTED RATHER THAN RESERVED

    -XX:+AlwaysPreTouch makes the JVM touch every page of the heap at startup, so
    an exit status of 0 is evidence the host COMMITTED 64 GiB rather than merely
    reserved address space for it. The heap used for the invocation is exactly
    this floor, so no larger value needs its own proof - the direction of the rule
    is that raising a heap is permitted and reported, and lowering one produces a
    truncated graph whose silence cannot be told from a clean result.
$ JAVA_HOME="$JAVA_HOME_21" PATH="$JAVA_HOME_21/bin:$PATH" java -Xms64g -Xmx64g -XX:+AlwaysPreTouch -version; echo "commit proof exit=$?  (0 = the host COMMITTED a 64 GiB heap, pre-touched, not merely reserved it)"
