================================================================================
PHASE 5 - THE SECOND PAIR, AND THE PARAMETERIZABILITY PROOF
================================================================================

  This is the phase the file exists for. Parameterizability is the one effort
  measure with a built-in temptation to cheat, because a query that ACCEPTS
  parameters looks parameterized. The measure's pass condition closes that door:
  it passes ONLY where the parameterized query is actually invoked on the second
  named pair - the StandaloneRestServer handler to the DriverRunner sink - and
  that invocation's result is captured in the query's result files. A parameter
  list that merely exists does not satisfy it, and an empty result from a REAL
  invocation does.

  So the evidence below is an invocation, not a claim. The second pair was
  invoked inside the same run as the first, in the declared order, and its own
  selection, walk counters, boundary measurements, distinct-route count and
  spurious count are all published - which is what makes the measure answerable
  by a reader who does not trust this file.
