PHASE 8 - THE SPURIOUS-ROUTE DEFINITION, AND ITS SELECTORS VERBATIM
================================================================================

  "Spurious" is a word that means whatever the person using it wants unless it is
  defined mechanically, so the query defines it mechanically and this file quotes
  the definition rather than paraphrasing it. THE DEFINITION JUDGES THE QUERY,
  NOT SPARK: it asks whether a route the query returned passed an authorization or
  ACL predicate on its way to the sink, which is a question about the query's own
  precision.

  8.1 THE BLOCK VERBATIM, from the query source

