  10.2 THIS FILE'S BYTE SIZE AND SHA256

    Owned by oss-scan-results/run-record.md, which holds the manifest of both
    artifact trees with a byte size and a sha256 per file, this one included. They
    are deliberately NOT written here: a digest of a file cannot appear inside
    that file, because writing it changes the bytes it describes. The manifest
    owner measures this file after it is closed, which is why the measurement
    lives there and is referenced from here.

    Both artifact trees are excluded from git's ordinary collection by
    .gitignore:31 (artifacts/), which is why publication is by that manifest
    rather than by the tree being collected. This particular path is ALREADY
    TRACKED - an earlier lane force-added it - so the update to it stages under a
    plain add, while a newly created file beside it would still need an explicit
    one. git check-ignore attributes the exclusion to .gitignore:31 for any
    untracked path under harness/artifacts/, which is the rule this file's
    publication route depends on.

