  10.4 THE ONE THING A READER SHOULD TAKE FROM THIS FILE

    The parameterized query was invoked on both named pairs, in one run, and the
    second pair - the REST submit servlet's handleSubmit reaching the same
    privileged launch - returned a measured, empty route set under a bound it
    reached, with its own entry point, its own walk counters and its own five
    boundaries. That is what makes parameterizability a measurement here rather
    than a claim. Everything else in this file exists so that the claim can be
    checked without trusting it: the graph's identity re-verified before the load,
    the target surface measured at the pin, the heap proven committed, the
    selectors quoted verbatim, the sibling verdicts read from the siblings' own
    envelopes, and the one transcription that no longer matches its source named
    with both values instead of quietly fixed.

